.TH IO_SETUP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
io_setup \- creates a linux kernel asynchronous i/o context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/aio.h>
.B int io_setup(unsigned int max_events, aio_context_t* context);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a Linux kernel asynchronous I/O context. The context must initially be zero and must be released with io_destroy. This is the Linux kernel AIO ABI, not POSIX aio.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_setup (2)
